        content: "The Unseen Poem (20 marks) tests your ability to analyse a poem you've never seen before. You have about 20 minutes.\n\nStep-by-step approach:\n1. Read the poem three times:\n   - First reading: Get the overall meaning and feeling. What is it about?\n   - Second reading: Look for techniques and patterns. What do you notice?\n   - Third reading: Focus on specific lines and words. What stands out?\n\n2. Consider the basics:\n   - Subject: What is the poem about? (Literal level)\n   - Theme: What deeper idea is being explored? (Figurative level)\n   - Speaker: Who is speaking? What is their perspective/attitude?\n   - Audience: Who is being addressed?\n   - Tone: What is the emotional atmosphere? Does it change?\n   - Structure: How is the poem organised? Stanzas, line length, rhyme?\n\n3. Identify techniques:\n   - Imagery: What pictures are created? What senses are engaged?\n   - Figurative language: Metaphor, simile, personification, symbolism.\n   - Sound devices: Alliteration, assonance, consonance, onomatopoeia, rhyme.\n   - Structural devices: Enjambment, caesura, stanza breaks, line length variation.\n   - Repetition: Words, phrases, or structures that recur.\n   - Contrast: Opposing ideas, images, or tones.\n\n4. Write your response:\n   - Answer the specific question asked.\n   - Use short, integrated quotes from the poem.\n   - Name techniques and explain their EFFECT.\n   - Don't just identify - analyse. Say WHY the poet uses this technique and what it ACHIEVES.",
