        content: "All extended writing in LC English is assessed using the PCLM criteria. Understanding these helps you know exactly what examiners are looking for.\n\nP - Clarity of Purpose (30 marks):\n- Have you understood and fulfilled the task?\n- Is your response focused and sustained?\n- Do you show clear engagement with the question/topic?\n- Is your purpose clear throughout (to argue, narrate, describe, analyse, persuade)?\nHow to maximise: State your purpose/position clearly in your introduction. Every paragraph should serve your overall purpose. Stay on topic.\n\nC - Coherence of Delivery (30 marks):\n- Is your response well-structured and organised?\n- Do your paragraphs flow logically from one to the next?\n- Is there a clear introduction, development, and conclusion?\n- Are transitions smooth and effective?\nHow to maximise: Plan before writing. Use topic sentences. Link paragraphs with transition words. Each paragraph = one main idea.\n\nL - Efficiency of Language Use (30 marks):\n- Is your vocabulary varied and appropriate?\n- Are your sentences varied in length and structure?\n- Is your style appropriate to the task (formal for essay, conversational for speech)?\n- Do you use literary/rhetorical devices effectively?\nHow to maximise: Avoid repeating the same words. Mix short and long sentences. Use specific vocabulary, not vague words. Show range.\n\nM - Accuracy of Mechanics (10 marks):\n- Is your spelling accurate?\n- Is your grammar correct?\n- Is your punctuation used properly?\n- Is your tense consistent?\nHow to maximise: Proofread. Check apostrophes, comma splices, and tense consistency. If unsure of a spelling, use a different word.",
